pert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Hawaii remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of 13 points toward Democrats. The 2028 contest is an open-seat race: the incumbent Republican president is term-limited, so neither side carries an incumbency advantage, and the state's underlying lean is the dominant factor. No candidate-specific fundraising, polling, or expert ratings exist yet for the general election, leaving the picture unusually bare for a presidential state.\n\nWith no polls or ratings to lean on, uncertainty is high even though the direction clearly favors Democrats. Hawaii has reliably supported the Democratic nominee across national environments, and recent coverage contains no sign of a competitive Republican operation there. The likely outcome is a Democratic win with a double-digit margin, though the exact size is difficult to pin down before candidates are settled and polling begins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9253, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8703, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9295, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8784, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.877, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.874, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8862, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.878, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8743, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8792, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8767, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07"